  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The sideways-climbing repair is installed. The old path could wait forever for a narrow-ledge dictionary/phase that never became executable, leaving lateral gain at zero. It now makes one bounded narrow-ledge attempt, switches to the known executable Story cliff-traverse fallback if loading/progress fails, and measures actual lateral travel instead of treating a timeout as proof. Test A/D and stick in both directions plus reversal; movement must travel tangent to the wall, and the log must show at least 0.05 m actual movement rather than only a requested animation.",
